--TEST--
A value an `Ldap\Entry` returns is `tainted`, so `string`'s result does not compile as a search `base` — ADR 0278 § 5 and § 6 and `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Reports {
    public static function under(Core\Ldap\Connection $corp, Core\Ldap\Entry $manager): void {
        var $base = $manager->string("distinguishedName");
        if ($base != null) {
            var $found = $corp->search(Core\Ldap\Filter::present("cn"), {base: $base});
        }
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:6:80
%A
  = help: `base` is a sink and no `Core` member launders one for it: the only way through is `Core\Taint::assertTrusted($value, $reason)`, which is forbidden by default, greppable, and carries in the source the reason the value can be trusted

